{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401186-why-where-the-maeghar-unable-to-continue-embrace-other-maeghar","id":1401186,"title":"Why where the Maeghar unable to continue embrace other Maeghar?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-05T13:53:08-07:00","id":1401186,"title":"Why where the Maeghar unable to continue embrace other Maeghar?","content":"Like in the title, why can the Maeghar not embrace other Maeghar when they have no feyblood after Marconius meddling? During the Dark Ages the Fey Blood where only a needing so that a none Kiasyd can embrace another person with feyblood to a Kiasyd. The Kiasyd where able to embrace other Kiasyd despite no feyblood. So how or why are the Maeghar not able to embrace other non Feybloods anymore since the rise of Marconius?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T09:58:31-07:00","id":1401504,"title":"","content":"I think Maeghar were never able to actually embrace another maeghar. at least not always, right? Not all maeghar were embraced by a maeghar, some were sired by a vampire with a clan, but... something went wrong and they became maeghar. So They are kinda like a caitiff, a specific kind of caitiff, related to feyblood. Thus they can only create another like them if everything goes wrong the right way. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I might be wrong, it has been a long time since i've read that v20 book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T11:13:34-07:00","id":1401516,"title":"","content":"Well technically you are right because the Maeghar are only calling themselves after the sheme of Marconius. Before they where all Kiasyd and in the DAV20 it is said, that they where able to embrace other Kiasyd. So this is what confuses me. During the Dark Ages Kiasyd can embrace other into Kiasyd no matter if Feyblood or not. But after Marconius meddling only those that stay loyal to him can keep embracing like this while those that want nothing to do with him and so calling themselves Maeghar only make Kiasyd if they are of the Fey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T08:43:50-07:00","id":1401698,"title":"","content":"Here is how I understand it.<br /> <br /> Originally Kiasyd was the moniker for any vampire that had a connection to the fae as a mortal. If they were able to survive and go on later to embrace, their childer would also be Kiasyd IF they also had a far connection, otherwise they would simply be Caitiff.<br /> <br /> Then Marconius comes along, by all accounts, perhaps a true Kiasyd, perhaps a mage that did wacky experiments with melding blood. Regardless, his efforts make him a Kiasyd, and he decides, his will be the only Kiasyd game in town. He can directly embrace fellow Kiasyd because of the nature of his creation; as an experiment. He claims the title Kiasyd, and those that are not of his blood say &quot;Sure, what's in a name?&quot; and take the name Maeghar. The Maeghar still need that connection to the fae as a mortal to present as Maeghar upon embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T12:12:23-07:00","id":1402444,"title":"","content":"Originally, &quot;Kiasyd&quot; was a term used to describe any faerie-blooded vampire, whether they had successfully survived the trauma of the Embrace or otherwise been transformed by the touch of faerie. These vampires instinctively knew that they did not belong, and most sires immediately disposed of their &quot;freak accidents&quot;. Those rare Kiasyd that survived found that they could pass on their curse with the Embrace, creating new Kiasyd. Most of these Kiasyd lineages were scattered, as most Kiasyd could not stand close contact, as it reminded them of what they had lost.<br /> This changed around the beginning of the Renaissance, as Marconius and his brood sought to rule alone, and other Kiasyd started to disappear. The surviving Kiasyd surrendered their name and disputed territory, renaming themselves the Maeghar, leaving Marconius' bloodline as the only Kiasyd.<br /> <br /> In the modern nights, Maeghar are solitary wanderers who travel from place to place, having no real ties to mortals or Kindred. They avoid the Sabbat and Marconius' Kiasyd brood. Typically, they will have a single prized, and disturbing, collection of some small item like children's teeth, finger bones, or broken dreams.<br /> <br /> Marconius brood is a bit different than the original Kiasyds who became the Maeghar; the historical accounts of the creation of the Kiasyd point to a trio of Lasombra who haphazardly delved into the roots of Obtenebration. The three vampires acquired through trade with a traveling wizard something labeled &quot;the blood of Zeernebooch, god of the Underworld&quot;. What was actually in the bottle no one knows for sure, but the three Lasombra assumed it was what the wizard said it was and mixed it in with the blood of a captured Unseelie fae. The Kiasyd themselves claim that Marconius was a mortal mage before the Embrace, who specialized in alchemy and worked together with his sister Hrotsuitha to create a perfect being. Marconius drank the potion and rapidly changed: growing taller, thinner, and even paler. His eyes changed to orbs of inky black, his skin became a glowing chalk white, and his features took on a pronounced fae appearance. The Kiasyd themselves claim that Hrotsuitha dabbled in Abyss Mysticism and that Marconius entered the Abyss itself and devoured his sister, changing himself in the process.<br /> Marconius and his &quot;Kiasyd&quot; are a result of a Mage medling with diferent kind of supernatural blood, including potent fae blood, and the whole accident happened far from the eyes og god and man, in the Abyss, created a whole new breed, like how the Nagaraja and House Tremere came to be, while the Maeghar/original Kiasyd were the result of an accident, when a vampire embraced a fea blooded human/changeling and only could make another Original Kiasyd when they were embraced a similar fae blooded (a normal human resulted a normal vampire) <br /> Only the Mytherceria signitrue discipline (thanks to the fea blood) and the weird look was common in the two lines<br /> <br /> The lack of new Maeghar is the result of two things : they never were eager to embrace to begin with, and in the modern nights the World lost its connection to the dreaming, and fewer and fewer changeling born, thus the chance became very low - except if you actively hunt them to embrace - to run in to one and bring them in the blood, creating an offspring","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T13:10:34-07:00","id":1402450,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm looking at the OP and thinking 'What? They can't do that?' <br /> <br /> The Maeghar aren't one line, they're not a group, they're just what happens when you embrace a Changeling (or once-changeling or whatever). The Kiasyd have no connections to curse Maeghar with; It's the other way round: The Kiasyd on the otherhand are a propper bloodline; you'll have to be looking at 'How bloodlines are made&quot; to answer why they've passed down the Mytherceria/Obtenebration/Dominate spread; Basically the OG Kiasyd has warped and calcified his blood to have a bloodline, whilst the Maeghar are a fleeting mutation. Perhaps, were a Maeghar to lower their generation and Gain a strong disposition towards a few disciplines and metaphysically earn a weakness, they too would make another Fae bloodline. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T14:22:13-07:00","id":1402467,"title":"","content":"Again you people are not understanding what I mean. In the Dark Ages the Kiasyd where less a bloodline and more a collection of those feybloods that survived the embrace and their children because those feyblood vampires can make other feyblood vampires no matter if the target has feyblood or not.<br /> <br /> Then came Marconius and the Kiasyd split up to those that followed him and where still called Kiasyd and where still able to embrace Fayvampires no matter if the target has feyblood or not<br /> and the Maeghar that keep themselves away from their former clansiblings and for other Maeghar embracing their target need to have Feyblood or it will become a Caitiff.<br /> <br /> Now my question is, how did it come, that during the dark ages everyone whas able to embrace Kiasyd no matter if Feyblood or not while now only those with Marconius can?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T17:37:33-07:00","id":1402500,"title":"","content":"Honest answer, nobody knows. The blood changed somehow. Might have something to do with Marconius using blood sorcery to bind the kiasyd name to his line, mystically castrating other kiasyd in the process. But that would only be headcanon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T19:26:56-07:00","id":1402513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401186-why-where-the-maeghar-unable-to-continue-embrace-other-maeghar?p=1402467#post1402467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again you people are not understanding what I mean. In the Dark Ages the Kiasyd where less a bloodline and more a collection of those feybloods that survived the embrace and their children because those feyblood vampires can make other feyblood vampires no matter if the target has feyblood or not.<br /> <br /> Then came Marconius and the Kiasyd split up to those that followed him and where still called Kiasyd and where still able to embrace Fayvampires no matter if the target has feyblood or not<br /> and the Maeghar that keep themselves away from their former clansiblings and for other Maeghar embracing their target need to have Feyblood or it will become a Caitiff.<br /> <br /> Now my question is, how did it come, that during the dark ages everyone whas able to embrace Kiasyd no matter if Feyblood or not while now only those with Marconius can?</div> </div> </div> </div>OOC answer, it's a change in mechanics between the editions. Same as how a Quietus power in V20 core is an Obfuscate power in DAV20 core. I don't think an IC explanation was ever provided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T02:27:33-07:00","id":1402548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401186-why-where-the-maeghar-unable-to-continue-embrace-other-maeghar?p=1402513#post1402513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OOC answer, it's a change in mechanics between the editions. Same as how a Quietus power in V20 core is an Obfuscate power in DAV20 core. I don't think an IC explanation was ever provided.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that was the result of a writer -not getting it-. And while in V5 they corrected a little and established the quiet movement as a mental trick like the rest of obfuscate, DAV20 didn't do that, and replaced Quietus 1 with an utterly absurd power of converting hearts into jars. DAV20 was truly an interesting time for discipline changes; Some great things, some atrocities. <br /> <br /> <br /> I would hazard to guess that back then, Fae were embraced with low generation, so they would pass on their traits. Then they were slaughtered. Now, Fae are embraced with high generation, so their blood isn't ready to make a bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}